{
 "slug": "test/material-measurement-inputs",
 "about": "A material measurement's own dimensions (Store B, the analyzer's material inputs) and its notes: taken from the Settings defaults (Store A) when the measurement completes, from the file on a load — which never writes the Settings defaults — and written by a save. Each case starts a fresh analyzer and runs its 'steps' in order: {\"settings\": {...}} sets those settings as Settings does (names as Swift's TapDisplaySettings; 'measurementType' and 'plateStiffnessPreset' by their saved names); {\"complete\": true} marks the measurement complete, as a capture does; {\"loading\": bool} sets whether a load is in progress; {\"clearInputs\": true} clears the measurement's dimensions; {\"hasInputs\": bool} checks whether it has them (a precondition); {\"load\": file, \"notes\"?: text} loads that inline file, with its notes replaced when 'notes' is given; {\"save\": true} builds the record a save writes. 'expect' after the last step: 'inputs' (null, or the measurement's dimensions — lengthMM, widthMM, thicknessMM, massG, bodyLengthMM, bodyWidthMM, stiffnessPreset by its saved name, customStiffness — only those named are checked), 'settings' (those settings' values), 'saved' (those fields of the saved record's longitudinal snapshot, 'guitarType' by its saved name), 'loadedNotes' (the notes a re-save would start from, null for none). Expected values are Swift's.",
